k and his team gave the proposal presentation today. While the teacher didn't have any comments, the teaching assistant gave them some feedback, which was not constructive criticism and they didn't find it helpful as it felt like he didn't understand their presentation.\n\n## Question \nIn this scenario, what is the most effective Response for Frank?\n\n## Choices\nA) \"We appreciate your feedback, is there any chance we could discuss further?\"\nB) \"Can we ask for feedback from a person who listened to the presentation?\"\nC) \"Thank you, we really appreciate your feedback. We'll work on what you pointed out.\"\nD) \"We don't think you fully understood our presentation\"","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.003172316445894531,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e8b1d6006945d280a0ee","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369713577,"createTime":"2026-11-11 12:01:53","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"a3e36038dde4441889cfee95b6257024"}